1790603691.900	
1790603691.900	The story of the printing press is not a single, monolithic event but rather a centuries-long evolution—a gradual convergence of metallurgy, mechanical engineering, chemical understanding, and societal demand. It is a narrative spanning from ancient woodblock techniques to Gutenberg’s movable type revolution in Mainz, and subsequently through the industrialization of print that defined the modern era. To trace this history is to chart the trajectory of modernity itself: from localized dogma to global discourse.
